# Knowledge base hygiene

- Treat `todo.md` as short-term memory (Session + Now/Next/Done). Update it when finishing a task.
- Treat `docs/` as current truth. Prefer `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/runbook.md`, `docs/decisions.md` over chat history.
- Treat `idea.md` as vision only — do not implement or document aspirational agents as if they already exist.
- One home per fact: update the matching file; link elsewhere instead of duplicating.
- When a lasting choice changes (provider, CLI contract, layout), append or supersede an entry in `docs/decisions.md`.
- Do not invent env vars, commands, or modules missing from code + docs.
